From 16d571d6ad027b6816482ec6f2a68aefbe62fc3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 04:08:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 140/146] hydra: nodes inside a nested nodegraph keep their
 path

A node placed in a NodeGraph (which is what every Houdini material subnetwork
writes) arrives from Hydra named by its path under the material, "G/a".
MaterialNodeNameToSdfPath made it a child of the root, which a name containing
"/" cannot be: empty path for all these nodes, which ended up merged into one
("Graph connect: input already connected" by the hundreds) and the network
rendered a constant. The name is now read as a relative path.

Measured on the MtlX Text node as a subnetwork (1107 nodes): before, all its
outputs wrong on 100 % of pixels; after, test_render 0 pixels off the numpy
reference, test_lop 0, test_features at most 0.09 % (edges). bench_mtlx: 93
cases, 0 problems (new nodegraph_nested case, failing before); bench_hair: 4
pairs, 0 problems.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hydra/material.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/hydra/material.cpp b/src/hydra/material.cpp
index 203dc23c..efdc6b0b 100644
--- a/src/hydra/material.cpp
+++ b/src/hydra/material.cpp
@@ -54,6 +54,12 @@ static SdfPath MaterialNodeNameToSdfPath(const TfToken &nodeName)
   if (s[0] == '/' && SdfPath::IsValidPathString(s)) {
     return SdfPath(s);
   }
+  /* A node inside a nodegraph (a Houdini material subnet) is named by its
+   * path below the material, "graph/node": a single child name cannot hold
+   * the slash, and every such node fell on the empty path, wired into one. */
+  if (s.find('/') != std::string::npos && SdfPath::IsValidPathString(s)) {
+    return SdfPath::AbsoluteRootPath().AppendPath(SdfPath(s));
+  }
   return SdfPath::AbsoluteRootPath().AppendChild(nodeName);
 }
 
